  "repo_truth": "After the CLEAN repository-identity selector review and exact helper implementation, standalone Stage 10 preview/apply and raw compile-payload refusal pass. The happy/skip M4 journeys now reach the Work Specification compile header, where two stale test literals fail. M5 reaches handoff emission, which correctly derives example-record-work from the two foundation-flow model outputs' generic record_id. The committed M4 expected plan, scorecard, transcript, bundle root, consumer path, and test constant all preserve fs-m4-foundation-journey-2026-04. No production failure is observed.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Read-only replay of all 18 manifest entries and the exact selector-amendment diff.",
    "Trace feature-ID derivation from Work Specification record_id through handoff and the M4 consumer harness.",
    "Validate whether changing only the two foundation-flow model-output record_id values preserves the existing M4 proof identity and is smaller than changing downstream expected proof assets.",
    "Validate that the shared pipeline proof corpus and every other Work Specification field remain unchanged.",
    "Apply the 04 reviewability indicators and identify findings independently before comparing P3/P4 candidates with 09."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No edits, formatting, staging, commit, push, handoff, ledger, dispatch, or delegation.",
    "No production/runtime, handoff logic, renderer, shared pipeline fixture, expected generated view, scorecard, expected slice plan, public API, dependency, Cargo/version, unsafe-policy, P2, P4, P5, P6, or sibling-slice change.",
    "Do not review or approve future fixture bytes or the broader P3B implementation delta."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Verify complete subject identity and inspect the exact selector-amendment delta.",
    "Independently trace the actual M5 feature ID and bundle root to the Work Specification record_id.",
    "Determine whether the exact two one-line fixture changes are necessary, sufficient, minimal, and semantically correct for the established M4 proof identity.",
    "Check whether any downstream expected proof asset would still require a material change after preserving the existing feature ID.",
    "Return findings first in Critical, Required, Optional, Nit order with exact file/line, violated contract, why wrong, smallest remediation, and missing verification."
  ],
  "contracts_and_gates": [
    "P3 canonical Work Specification and handoff derivation remain unchanged",
    "M4 stable feature identity remains fs-m4-foundation-journey-2026-04",
    "Only two foundation-flow Work Specification record_id lines may change",
    "Shared pipeline proof corpus and downstream expected proof assets remain unchanged",
    "No production symbol or broader schema inference is authorized"
  ],
  "stop_conditions": [
    "Return blocked if subject identity or required read-only evidence cannot be established.",
